.TH WMCLIPD 1 "2026" "Window Maker"
.SH NAME
wmclipd \- X11 clipboard daemon for Window Maker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmclipd
[\fB\-\-clipboard\fR] [\fB\-\-screenshots\fR] [\fB\-\-history\fR\ \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-ttl\fR\ \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB\-\-persist\fR] [\fB\-\-history\-file\fR\ \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR]
.br
.B wmclipd
\fB\-\-help\fR|\fB\-h\fR
.br
.B wmclipd
\fB\-\-version\fR|\fB\-v\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmclipd
runs as a user-started X11 clipboard helper. In clipboard mode it monitors
the CLIPBOARD and PRIMARY selections and preserves supported text and image
payloads after the original owner exits. In screenshot mode it subscribes to
Window Maker screenshot IPC events and publishes each saved screenshot to the
CLIPBOARD selection.
.PP
When clipboard history is enabled (the default), wmclipd keeps a ring of the
last
.I N
captured entries and can show a popup list to pick from the history. The popup
is triggered by a Window Maker keybinding that sends a WIPC tick event; see
the
.B CLIPBOARD POPUP
section below. Entries can additionally be expired after a fixed age with
.BR \-\-ttl .
Capturing an entry already in the ring moves the existing entry to the front
and refreshes its age while preserving its pin state. Entries match only if
their content type, bytes, and any path and URI metadata match.
.PP
Screenshot payloads are offered as
.B image/png
or
.B image/jpeg
when the saved file uses one of those formats, and also as
.B text/uri-list
and text path targets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-clipboard
Run as an X11 clipboard manager for CLIPBOARD and PRIMARY.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print runtime diagnostics to standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit. The short
.B \-h
alias is also accepted.
.TP
.B \-\-history N
Keep the last
.I N
clipboard entries in an in-memory history ring (default 10, 0 disables).
History is active whenever
.B \-\-clipboard
or
.B \-\-screenshots
runs. Setting
.I N
to 0 reverts to the single-slot legacy mode. Entries larger than 16 MiB are
kept as the live selection but are not added to the ring.
.TP
.BI \-\-history\-file " PATH"
Store the persistent history in
.I PATH
instead of the default location. Implies
.BR \-\-persist .
.TP
.B \-\-persist
Save the history ring to disk on clean exit and restore it on the next start.
See the
.B PERSISTENCE
section below.
.TP
.B \-\-screenshots
Subscribe to Window Maker screenshot IPC events and publish saved screenshots
to CLIPBOARD.
The singular
.B \-\-screenshot
is accepted as an alias.
.TP
.BI \-\-ttl " DURATION"
Remove history entries older than
.IR DURATION .
The duration is a number followed by a unit:
.B s
(seconds),
.B m
(minutes),
.B h
(hours) or
.B d
(days); a bare number means seconds and combinations such as
.B 1h30m
are accepted. The smallest enabled duration is
.B 5s
and the largest is
.BR 365d .
The default
.B 0
disables expiry. Pinned entries are exempt from expiry, matching capacity
eviction, and re-copying the same content restarts that entry's timer.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit. The short
.B \-v
alias is also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B wmclipd --clipboard
Run only the clipboard manager with the default history ring (10 entries).
.TP
.B wmclipd --clipboard --history 0
Run the clipboard manager in legacy single-slot mode (no history popup).
.TP
.B wmclipd --clipboard --history 20 --ttl 1h
Keep 20 entries and drop each one an hour after it was captured.
.TP
.B wmclipd --clipboard --ttl 10m
Keep the default ring of 10 entries, dropping each 10 minutes after it was
captured.
.TP
.B wmclipd --clipboard --persist --ttl 1d
Keep the default ring for a day and restore it across logouts and restarts.
.TP
.B wmclipd --screenshots
Copy Window Maker screenshots to CLIPBOARD without monitoring normal clipboard
changes.
.TP
.B wmclipd --clipboard --screenshots
Run the clipboard manager and replace CLIPBOARD with each new Window Maker
screenshot.
.PP
To start it with Window Maker, add a command such as:
.EX
wmclipd --clipboard --screenshots &
.EE
to
.BR ~/.config/WindowMaker/Library/WindowMaker/autostart .
.SH PERSISTENCE
By default the history ring lives in memory only and every restart starts
empty. With
.BR \-\-persist ,
the ring is written to a single binary state file on clean exit and restored
on the next start, keeping content, order, pin state, capture time and X
content type. A clean exit is
.B SIGTERM
or
.B SIGINT
(as sent by the login manager at session logout) or an X server disconnect.
A crash or
.B SIGKILL
loses the history.
.PP
Because clipboard history regularly contains passwords and other secrets,
persistence is opt-in. The state file is created with mode
.B 0600
inside a
.B 0700
directory, by default
.IB $XDG_STATE_HOME /WindowMaker/wmclipd-history
(fallback
.IR ~/.local/state/WindowMaker/wmclipd-history ).
If an existing history file cannot be read or is invalid, it is left unchanged
and history saving is disabled for that session.
Screenshot entries whose backing file no longer exists at load time are
dropped, and non-pinned entries whose
.B \-\-ttl
has already passed are skipped. Restored entries do not re-claim the live
CLIPBOARD selection, ownership stays session-local.
.PP
In the popup, entries captured on a previous day are labelled with the
weekday and day (for example
.IR "Fri 26 17:03" )
instead of a bare time.
.SH "CLIPBOARD POPUP"
When history is enabled, wmclipd subscribes to Window Maker IPC tick events
and shows a popup list of the history ring when it receives a tick with the
payload
.IR wmclipd-popup .
The popup is wired to a Window Maker keybinding through two defaults in the
WindowMaker domain:
.TP
.B ClipboardKey
Keybinding that triggers the clipboard popup (default
.IR Mod4+v ).
.TP
.B ClipboardCommand
Command run when
.B ClipboardKey
is pressed (default
.IR "wmakermsg send_tick wmclipd-popup" ).
Any clipboard manager can be invoked this way.
.SS "Popup keys"
.TP
.B v
Advance selection to the next entry (wrap around).
.TP
.BR Up / Down " or " k / j
Move selection to the previous or next entry.
.TP
.BR Home / End
Jump to the first or last entry.
.TP
.BR PageUp / PageDown
Scroll the list by one viewport.
.TP
.B p
Toggle a pin on the current entry. Pinned entries are exempt from capacity
eviction, from
.B \-\-ttl
expiry and from the clear-all key; they are shown with a pin marker.
.TP
.B b
Encode the selected entry as a Base64 data URI and publish it as UTF-8 text
to CLIPBOARD and PRIMARY without adding the generated URI to history.
The original stored input is limited to 1 MiB. PNG and JPEG bytes are
encoded unchanged. UTF-8 text is validated, STRING is converted from
Latin-1, and TEXT and COMPOUND_TEXT are decoded as compound text.
Invalid or unsupported text is rejected without changing either selection.
.IP
After the popup closes, wmclipd submits Shift+Insert to the previously
focused window, even for an image entry. If an invocation modifier is still
held, submission waits until it is released while clipboard and IPC events
continue to be processed. The pending paste is cancelled if either generated
selection is lost, the target becomes unusable, or another popup opens.
If publication succeeds but paste submission fails, the generated selections
remain available. If only one selection claim succeeds, the result is
reported on standard error and no paste key is sent. Key-event submission
does not confirm that the receiving application pasted the data.
.TP
.B s
Save the selected entry's original bytes under
.IB $XDG_DATA_HOME /WindowMaker/Clipboard/
(fallback
.IR ~/.local/share/WindowMaker/Clipboard/ ).
PNG and JPEG entries use
.B .png
and
.BR .jpg .
Text entries use
.B .txt
and retain their original encoding, which is not necessarily UTF-8.
The popup dismisses whether the action succeeds or fails. On success, the
absolute path is copied to CLIPBOARD and PRIMARY as UTF-8 text and as a percent-encoded
.B text/uri-list
with a CRLF terminator. No paste key is sent and the path is not added to
history. The original entry and history ordering are unchanged, even if all
entries are pinned. The saved file remains if the path is not UTF-8 or a
selection claim fails. If only one claim succeeds, that selection retains the
path. Partial successes and other errors are reported on standard error.
Exports can contain sensitive clipboard contents.
.TP
.B Delete
Remove the selected entry from the ring. The live CLIPBOARD selection is
unaffected. If no entries remain, the popup dismisses.
.TP
.BR "Shift+Delete"
Clear all non-pinned entries from the ring. The live CLIPBOARD selection is
unaffected. If no entries remain, the popup dismisses.
.TP
.B Return
Commit the selected entry to CLIPBOARD and dismiss.
.TP
.B Escape
Cancel and dismiss without changing CLIPBOARD.
.TP
.B "click"
Single-click on a row to commit that entry and dismiss.
.TP
.B "release modifier"
If a modifier key was held when the popup appeared, releasing any key that is
not a navigation, action, or modifier key commits the current selection
(matches Alt+Tab muscle memory). If no modifier was held (e.g. a modifier-less
keybinding), explicit Return or click is required.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X display used for the clipboard owner window and for resolving the Window
Maker IPC socket.
.TP
.B HOME
Fallback base for the state and export directories when the corresponding
XDG variable is unset or not absolute.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Absolute base directory for saved clipboard exports.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Absolute base directory for persistent history.
.TP
.B WMAKER_IPC_SOCKET
Overrides the Window Maker IPC socket path used by
.B \-\-screenshots .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
success,
.B 1
runtime failure,
.B 2
invalid command line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmaker (1),
.BR wmakermsg (1),
.BR wxcopy (1),
.BR wxpaste (1)
